{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Statutory right for domestic abuse victims to separate from joint mortgages",
        "additional_details": "Despite physically escaping abuse, the mortgage system can leave victims financially tied and exposed to the consequences of their abusers\u2019 actions. We want a statutory right where domestic abuse victims can unilaterally end their personal liability under a joint mortgage without their abuser\u2019s consent.\r\n \r\nI feel the experiences of domestic abuse victims show a wider gap in protection: survivors should not remain vulnerable to post-separation economic abuse through a joint mortgage. Leaving an abuser should mean freedom including financial freedom.",
        "background": "Create a statutory right for domestic abuse victims to unilaterally separate from joint mortgages, with specific protections against arrears, damaged credit and their abuser refusing to pay, sell or cooperate; ensuring a joint mortgage cannot be used as a tool of post-separation economic abuse.",
        "closed_at": null,
